            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 13-year-old boy presented with a 9-month history of episodic unilateral swelling of the face and oral pain. He reported having loose, nonbloody stools. Granulomatous inflammation consistent with Crohn's disease was found on histopathological examination.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
